Switch efficiently handles multiple conditions based on single value.

```c
on message 0x100 {
  byte msg_type = this.data[0];

  switch (msg_type) {
    case 0x01:
      write("Message type: Status");
      break;
    case 0x02:
      write("Message type: Error");
      break;
    case 0x03:
      write("Message type: Warning");
      break;
    default:
      write("Unknown message type: 0x%02X", msg_type);
      break;
  }
}
```

For loops iterate through fixed count, useful for processing array data.

```c
on message 0x100 {
  // Process all 8 data bytes
  for (int i = 0; i < this.dlc; i++) {
    write("Byte %d: 0x%02X", i, this.data[i]);
  }

  // Calculate checksum of all bytes
  byte checksum = 0;
  for (int j = 0; j < 7; j++) {
    checksum = checksum + this.data[j];
  }
  write("Calculated checksum: 0x%02X", checksum);
}
```

While loops continue until condition becomes false. Use with caution to avoid infinite loops.

```c
on start {
  int counter = 0;

  // Count up to 10
  while (counter < 10) {
    write("Counter: %d", counter);
    counter++;
  }

  // Accumulate data bytes
  byte accumulated = 0;
  int byte_index = 0;
  while (byte_index < 8) {
    accumulated = accumulated + (byte_index * 10);
    byte_index++;
  }
  write("Accumulated value: %d", accumulated);
}
```

Conditional operator for inline conditional assignment: condition ? true_value : false_value

```c
